cff-version: 1.3.0
title: "Image-Augmentation: a deterministic image mutation tool for reproducible datasets"
message: "If you use this tool in your research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Koka
    given-names: Vaishnav
repository-code: "https://github.com/vaishnavkoka/Image-Augmentation-tool"
license: MIT
version: 1.4.1
date-released: "2026-09-22"
keywords:
  - image augmentation
  - image mutation
  - reproducible research
  - dataset generation
  - ImageMagick
  - image provenance
abstract: >-
  A deterministic image augmentation and mutation tool built on ImageMagick.
  It exposes 76 operators through a web interface and an HTTP API, producing
  173 configurations per image. Output is byte-reproducible across runs and
  pixel-identical to the equivalent ImageMagick command line, so a generated
  corpus can be reproduced rather than archived. Thirteen validation suites
  check the operators against the reference implementation, the interface
  against the catalogue, and the server against operators that can crash it.
